Very well, then.

60
00:04:18,520 --> 00:04:21,400
Luke, I hate to ask, but would you deliver this?

61
00:04:21,500 --> 00:04:22,320
Certainly, sir.

62
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:26,200
The boy seems awfully hurried.

63
00:04:26,780 --> 00:04:29,020
I wonder if his errand has to do with our case.

64
00:04:30,060 --> 00:04:32,380
Do you think perhaps we ought to follow him?

65
00:04:33,020 --> 00:04:35,140
No, we're on no pressing schedule.

66
00:04:35,140 --> 00:04:37,720
I have a better idea in mind.

67
00:04:38,120 --> 00:04:49,040
It's been a long time since we could relax together like this, hasn't it?

68
00:04:49,640 --> 00:04:50,360
It has.

69
00:04:51,120 --> 00:04:53,380
It reminds me of our time with Lord Rockwell.

70
00:04:53,660 --> 00:04:55,660
That's the last I can remember bathing together.

71
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:58,560
But what should we do after this?

72
00:04:59,220 --> 00:04:59,960
What indeed?

73
00:05:00,760 --> 00:05:03,060
I'd like to meet with the painter as soon as possible.

74
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:05,740
There's something I would like to ask him.

75
00:05:06,560 --> 00:05:07,220
All right, then.

76
00:05:07,220 --> 00:05:10,260
I'll send a message to Lord Cupid once we leave.

77
00:05:10,460 --> 00:05:10,820
Stanley.

78
00:05:11,680 --> 00:05:11,960
Hmm?

79
00:05:12,600 --> 00:05:15,560
The painter I encountered in the slums all those years ago

80
00:05:15,560 --> 00:05:19,400
was a Mr. Stanley, not a Lord Cupid.

81
00:05:20,140 --> 00:05:20,640
What?

82
